WEBVTT

00:03:27.464 --> 00:03:30.163
What we noticed
is when the bacteria were alone,

00:03:30.187 --> 00:03:32.342
so when they were in dilute suspension,

00:03:32.366 --> 00:03:33.726
they made no light.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.798
But when they grew
to a certain cell number,

00:03:35.822 --> 00:03:39.172
all the bacteria turned on light
simultaneously.

00:03:39.196 --> 00:03:40.924
So the question that we had is:

00:03:40.948 --> 00:03:43.662
How can bacteria,
these primitive organisms,

00:03:43.686 --> 00:03:46.014
tell the difference
from times when they're alone

00:03:46.038 --> 00:03:47.929
and times when they're in a community,

00:03:47.953 --> 00:03:50.080
and then all do something together?

00:03:50.694 --> 00:03:54.795
And what we figured out is that the way
they do that is they talk to each other,

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:56.989
and they talk with a chemical language.

00:03:57.013 --> 00:03:59.726
So this is now supposed
to be my bacterial cell.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.248
When it's alone,
it doesn't make any light.